/// Controls how the layer is composited with the content already rendered
/// beneath it. Unlike per-feature opacity properties such as `fill-opacity`,
/// this property affects the final composited layer output and determines how
/// it interacts with the existing map contents.
///
/// ![fill-layer-blend examples](assets/fill-layer-blend.svg)
///
/// {@category Style}
/// {@subCategory Style Layers}
enum FillLayerBlend implements StyleEnum {
  /// [Normal](https://www.w3.org/TR/compositing-1/#blendingnormal) blending. The
  /// layer is drawn on top of existing content using standard alpha compositing.
  normal('normal'),

  /// [Multiply](https://www.w3.org/TR/compositing-1/#blendingmultiply) blending.
  /// The layer color is multiplied with the colors underneath, producing darker
  /// results. Useful for textures, hillshades, and combining raster and vector
  /// content.
  multiply('multiply'),

  /// [Color](https://www.w3.org/TR/compositing-1/#blendingcolor) blending.
  /// Creates a color with the hue and saturation of the layer and the luminosity
  /// of the content underneath, preserving its gray levels. Useful for tinting
  /// monochrome content such as a hillshade.
  color('color'),

  /// [Luminosity](https://www.w3.org/TR/compositing-1/#blendingluminosity)
  /// blending. Creates a color with the luminosity of the layer and the hue and
  /// saturation of the content underneath. The inverse of `color`.
  luminosity('luminosity'),

  /// [Plus-lighter](https://www.w3.org/TR/compositing-1/#porterduffcompositingoperators_plus)
  /// blending. Additive blending. The layer color is added to the colors
  /// underneath, producing brighter results. Useful for glow and heat
  /// accumulation effects.
  plusLighter('plus-lighter'),

  /// [Screen](https://www.w3.org/TR/compositing-1/#blendingscreen) blending. The
  /// inverse of the colors is multiplied, producing lighter results. Useful for
  /// glow, heatmap, and light-based effects.
  screen('screen'),

  /// [Overlay](https://www.w3.org/TR/compositing-1/#blendingoverlay) blending.
  /// Multiplies or screens colors depending on the colors underneath, preserving
  /// highlights and shadows while adding contrast.
  overlay('overlay');

  const FillLayerBlend(this.value);

  @override
  final String value;
}

